meta {
  name: POST /v1/chat/completions (recall-paged, reviewer helper)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "audittrace-default",
    "messages": [
      { "role": "user", "content": "{{recallPagedPrompt}}" }
    ],
    "stream": false,
    "max_tokens": 1024
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("OpenAI choices shape preserved (feedback_openai_schema_inviolate)", function() {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.choices).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body.choices[0].message.role).to.equal("assistant");
    expect(body.choices[0].message.content).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  Builder-added (ADR-059 loop, 2026-08-03 — backlog #15 residual, #375 /
  RECALL-PAGINATION-20260803): the recall-tool equivalent of
  `01b-list-paged.bru`. Recall tools (`recall_decisions`/`recall_skills`/
  `recall_semantic`/`recall_recent_sessions`) are NOT a standalone REST
  endpoint — they are invoked by the LLM inside the `/v1/chat/completions`
  tool-call loop — so this helper is a templated chat-completions call
  (same pattern as `02b-chat-completions-custom.bru`) whose `userPrompt`
  env var asks the model to page a recall tool forward.

  Set `recallPagedPrompt` to something like:

    "Call recall_decisions with query='<marker text>' and offset=0 first.
     If has_more is true, call it again with offset=5 (or offset += limit)
     until you find <marker text> or has_more is false. Report the total,
     has_more, and which offset surfaced it."

  This is what proves, through the real chat surface (not a direct tool
  invocation), that the tool SCHEMA alone teaches the model to page
  forward instead of re-issuing the same query (R3) — the exact failure
  mode that stalled a reviewer on 2026-08-02 (recall time-box `2b407e7`).

  For a deterministic, non-LLM-dependent proof of the same pagination
  mechanics, see `tests/test_memory_tool_handlers.py::
  TestRecallDecisionsPaginationEndToEnd` (invokes the tool handler
  directly against a seeded ChromaDB collection).
}
